Write a function read_log_file(filename) that:

Takes a string filename as input.

Attempts to open and read all lines from the file.

Uses a try-except block to gracefully handle two specific errors:

FileNotFoundError: Print a friendly message ("Error: Log file not found.") and return an empty list [].

PermissionError: Print a friendly message ("Error: You do not have permission to read this file.") and return an empty list [].

Uses a finally block to print "File access attempt completed." regardless of success or failure.


